unlicensed use and constitutes copyright infringement.

## 2. AGPL-3.0 PATH — COPYLEFT OBLIGATIONS

If you elect the AGPL-3.0 path:

  2.1 You must make the complete corresponding source of any work based on this
      software available to all users interacting with it over a network, per
      Section 13 of AGPL-3.0. For the avoidance of doubt: operating CLAI-OS,
      AEGIS-NG, or AEGIS-GLOBAL as a hosted clinical, safety, or governance
      service triggers this network-use clause.

  2.2 You must preserve all attribution notices naming Dr. Christabel Odeta as
      sole author, including repository headers, SPOS prompt metadata blocks,
      and SIP invocation banners.

  2.3 Modifications to the deterministic engine layer, the SIP routing tables,
      or the S50 checkpoint verification logic remain licensed under AGPL-3.0
      and must be disclosed in source form.

## 3. SAVANT-COMMERCIAL-1.0 PATH

If you elect the Savant-Commercial-1.0 path:

  3.1 Your rights, scope, seat/deployment limits, and fees are defined
      exclusively by your executed Commercial Access Agreement (CAA.md) and
      its accompanying order form.

  3.2 The commercial license never extends to the FHIR R4 resource layer. The
      FHIR R4 resource layer is and remains open under AGPL-3.0 in all
      distribution models. No commercial agreement may re-close it. The
      proprietary boundary is drawn at the deterministic engine layer only
      (see CAA.md, Section 3).

  3.3 Commercial licensees receive a limited, non-exclusive patent license to
      the subject matter of PPA-001 through PPA-005 strictly as embodied in
      the licensed software, for the term of the agreement.

## 4. PATENT RETALIATION CLAUSE

  4.1 If you, or any entity controlling, controlled by, or under common control
      with you, institute or join patent litigation against Dr. Christabel
      Odeta, the SAVANT FRAMEWORK project, or any contributor or licensee of
      this software, alleging that this software (or any contribution to it)
      infringes a patent, then all patent rights granted to you under this
      license — under BOTH the AGPL-3.0 path and the Savant-Commercial-1.0
      path — terminate automatically and immediately as of the date the
      litigation was first instituted.

  4.2 Termination under Section 4.1 does not terminate your copyright license
      under AGPL-3.0 (which is governed by AGPL-3.0 Section 8), but it does
      revoke any commercial patent covenant, defensive suspension benefit, or
      implied patent immunity you hold with respect to PPA-001 through
      PPA-005.

  4.3 A counterclaim filed purely in response to litigation first instituted
      by the Licensor does not trigger this clause.

## 5. SOVEREIGN TECHNOLOGY TRANSFER CARVE-OUT

  5.1 A sovereign nation, or a state-owned manufacturing or health authority
      acting under that nation's authority, that has received SAVANT FRAMEWORK
      blueprints, bills of materials, firmware images, or deployment
      documentation under a formal Sovereign Technology Transfer agreement is
      EXEMPT from all Savant-Commercial-1.0 license fees for non-commercial
      humanitarian deployment within its own territory.

  5.2 "Non-commercial humanitarian deployment" means deployment of AEGIS-NG
      units (reference per-unit cost USD 46.30), AEGIS-GLOBAL safety
      infrastructure, or CLAI-OS clinical reasoning systems where no fee is
      charged to end users and no component is resold, sublicensed, or
      exported for commercial advantage.

  5.3 The carve-out does not waive: (a) attribution obligations to
      Dr. Christabel Odeta; (b) the SHA-256 checkpoint integrity requirements
      of the S50 governance engine; (c) trademark restrictions in
      TRADEMARK.md; or (d) the copyleft obligations of AGPL-3.0 for modified
      source that is redistributed outside the receiving sovereign authority.

  5.4 Commercial exploitation by the receiving sovereign or its agents voids
      the exemption for the exploiting entity only, without prejudice to
      other sovereign parties.

